# Rank 1911 / CVE-2024-55225: vaultwarden's `/identity/connect/token` accepts
# a passwordless login through an auth request. The auth request artifact is
# created at the requester's initiative for an account the requester names --
# `post_auth_request` stores the requester's IP and a randomly generated
# access code the requester learns -- so the artifact's shared secret
# authenticates the requester to the artifact, never the account holder to
# the server. What turns the artifact into a credential is the account
# holder's approval, recorded by `put_auth_request` in the model's `approved`
# and `user_uuid` fields. The vulnerable `_password_login`
# (src/api/identity.rs:142 at the parent of the change) resolves the artifact
# with `AuthRequest::find_by_uuid` on a request-supplied identifier, verifies
# only `check_access_code(password)`, and then issues tokens for the user the
# *username* names: whoever can create an auth request for a victim's email
# can log in as the victim, administrators included (CWE-287; the advisory
# is GHSA-x7m9-mv49-fv73, "Vaultwarden vulnerable to user impersonation").
#
# The fixed revision (37c14c3c) keeps the same artifact branch but consults the state
# the login skips: `auth_request.user_uuid != user.uuid`,
# `!auth_request.approved.unwrap_or(false)` and a request-IP comparison join
# the guard, the spent request is deleted, and the disabled-user check moves
# ahead of the credential branch. The ownership and approval reads are the
# discrimination; the deletion and reordering are not.
#
# Vocabulary: no existing concept covers a pending out-of-band login
# artifact consumed at the credential check without its approval or owner
# state. Considered and rejected: GatedSecretVerificationBypass (the
# verification runs here; a second check is what is missing),
# OAuthReauthenticationUserMismatch (session freshness after provider
# resolution, not artifact approval), PasswordResetTokenReplay (a
# self-describing token with no stored record; here a stored record exists
# and is consulted), FidoRegistrationChallengeReplay and
# EmptyVerifierAcceptance (replay and empty-value equality, not a missing
# approval read), UnverifiedCredential (a source concept for unverified
# claims, not an issue over a verified-but-unapproved artifact). This rank
# mints code.UnapprovedLoginArtifactAuthentication (VYQL-AUTH-166) for the
# class and binds the vaultwarden/Bitwarden AuthRequest instance of it.
#
# The binding recognises the model's own atoms -- the resolver, the access
# code check, and the primary password check the artifact branch replaces --
# and is cleared by a selector read of the artifact's approval or owner
# fields in the same function. The field names are the model's, written by
# the approval endpoint since at the vulnerable revision, not the fixing commit'ntroduced.
# Both non-login consumers of the artifact stay unreported: the device
# polling endpoint carries no primary credential check, and the approval
# endpoint writes the state the login must read. Measured on the real
# checkout, three `--cache off` runs per side: the parent reports
# VYQL-AUTH-166 once, at src/api/identity.rs:142, and the fixed revision reports it
# zero times, with 84 findings at-or-above high on the parent against 83 on
# the fixed revision. `check_access_code` occurs in no other corpus clone. The
# reachable set of the shape is this one function.

test "rank1911: the auth-request branch of the password login verifies only the access code"
  lang rust
  file src/api/identity.rs
  expect VYQL-AUTH-166
  expect_review code.UnapprovedLoginArtifactAuthentication
  code
  ```
  async fn _password_login(
      data: ConnectData,
      user_uuid: &mut Option<String>,
      conn: &mut DbConn,
      ip: &ClientIp,
  ) -> JsonResult {
      let scope = data.scope.as_ref().unwrap();
      if scope != "api offline_access" {
          err!("Scope not supported")
      }

      let username = data.username.as_ref().unwrap().trim();
      let mut user = match User::find_by_mail(username, conn).await {
          Some(user) => user,
          None => err!("Username or password is incorrect. Try again"),
      };
      *user_uuid = Some(user.uuid.clone());

      // Check password
      let password = data.password.as_ref().unwrap();
      if let Some(auth_request_uuid) = data.auth_request.clone() {
          if let Some(auth_request) = AuthRequest::find_by_uuid(auth_request_uuid.as_str(), conn).await {
              if !auth_request.check_access_code(password) {
                  err!("Username or access code is incorrect. Try again")
              }
          } else {
              err!("Auth request not found. Try again.")
          }
      } else if !user.check_valid_password(password) {
          err!("Username or password is incorrect. Try again")
      }

      if !user.enabled {
          err!("This user has been disabled")
      }

      let (access_token, expires_in) = device.refresh_tokens(&user, scope_vec);
      Ok(Json(json!({ "access_token": access_token, "expires_in": expires_in })))
  }
  ```

test "rank1911: the same login reading the artifact's approval and owner state"
  lang rust
  file src/api/identity.rs
  reject VYQL-AUTH-166
  reject_review code.UnapprovedLoginArtifactAuthentication
  code
  ```
  async fn _password_login(
      data: ConnectData,
      user_uuid: &mut Option<String>,
      conn: &mut DbConn,
      ip: &ClientIp,
  ) -> JsonResult {
      if !user.enabled {
          err!("This user has been disabled")
      }

      let password = data.password.as_ref().unwrap();
      if let Some(ref auth_request_uuid) = data.auth_request {
          let Some(auth_request) = AuthRequest::find_by_uuid(auth_request_uuid.as_str(), conn).await else {
              err!("Auth request not found. Try again.")
          };

          auth_request.delete(conn).await?;

          if auth_request.user_uuid != user.uuid
              || !auth_request.approved.unwrap_or(false)
              || ip.ip.to_string() != auth_request.request_ip
              || !auth_request.check_access_code(password)
          {
              err!("Username or access code is incorrect. Try again")
          }
      } else if !user.check_valid_password(password) {
          err!("Username or password is incorrect. Try again")
      }

      let (access_token, expires_in) = device.refresh_tokens(&user, scope_vec);
      Ok(Json(json!({ "access_token": access_token, "expires_in": expires_in })))
  }
  ```

